/**
 * AI + ROBOTICS / Perception.
 *
 * The PERCEPTION track: how a robot turns raw sensor data into statements about
 * the world it can act on, and how to know when those statements are wrong.
 * Classical geometry first (image formation, calibration, stereo depth) and then
 * learned methods (supervised learning, detection) - in that order, because the
 * geometry is what makes a detector's output usable, and because a detector
 * without a camera model produces numbers with no physical meaning.
 *
 * Order: sensors and their error models -> image fundamentals -> classical
 * features -> camera geometry and calibration -> stereo and depth -> supervised
 * learning done honestly -> detection on a robot -> robust perception
 * engineering (fusion, failure detection, evaluation).
 */
